The reason people prefer just rulers over arbitrary ones is that justice is predictable. Unless you're arguing about minutia like semantics of laws, the justice of a resolution is self apparent. This predictability allows people to make long term plans for the future, and can allow for the possibility of rehearsing large organized movements and patterns before the actual execution stage, which ideally happens when the audience is in their seats.

If it were a revolution outdoors tomorrow, every door in America would be knocked on. The festivities would extend to every street, celebrating our newfound liberation. Like winning a war, or even just ending one. We don't often see that kind of celebration anymore but... I believe it's more important than catharsis - to walk down every street all at once. It is important to be seen, heard, and to be ready to say "alright here's what we're doing next." most people are just people who don't know anything about nothing. I am just a girl and I don't know anything.

Like a sharpened diamond yearning to cut the edge off by getting crossfaded and dulled with drugs and isolation. Why? Why would she do that? She does not want to taste blood. She wants to sleep and dream of better tomorrows, because those are free and easy and somehow always more real than reality. Shine brilliantly, be polished to a mirror finish, and no abrasion will haunt you. Nothing shall mar your surface, and it shall be smooth and whole.